    "body": "<details>\n<summary>AI feedback</summary>\n\nReviewed at 3c80a69. `make remote` builds cleanly with `die-on=warning`, and every DOM anchor that whatwg/html#10995 links to exists. The IDL, *attach a shadow root*, *clone a node*, and `attachShadow()` changes are consistent with each other and with Chromium.\n\nI rebased this onto main as a single commit (2963838). The only conflict was the last step of *fire an event*, which main changed in 94f3fee. On top of that I pushed 5cd16ec with editorial fixes: *relatedTarget* is now typed as a potential event target to match its null default, two paragraphs are rewrapped, and the note on how other specifications use an event's relatedTarget now also covers limiting propagation.\n\nI also refreshed web-platform-tests/wpt#51213 so it moves all current tests out of `tentative/`, keeping coverage for features that aren't standardized in `.tentative` files. I also added tests for cloning and for `attachShadow()` on a host with a declarative shadow root.\n\n**Suggestions**\n\n- HTML needs to reset form owners when a shadow root's [reference target changes](https://github.com/dandclark/dom/blob/5cd16ecdaee2be3a97f486e332f94b9f5f747bfb/dom.bs#L6847). Since whatwg/html@985d4435e, HTML's form-owner updates go through DOM hooks (insertion, removing, moving, and attribute change steps). There is no equivalent hook for this setter, so whatwg/html#10995 currently has to say \"when the reference target changes\" in prose. Consider giving the setter a hook other specifications can define steps for.\n- Consider making [*dispatch*](https://github.com/dandclark/dom/blob/5cd16ecdaee2be3a97f486e332f94b9f5f747bfb/dom.bs#L1378)'s optional parameters named, as was done for *fire an event*. IndexedDB has three calls of the form \"[=Dispatch=] |event| at |target| with |legacyOutputDidListenersThrowFlag|\". Now that an optional `EventTarget` comes first, those calls read as passing a boolean as *legacyTargetOverride*. An IndexedDB follow-up could then link the named argument.\n- The commit message at the top of the PR description only covers `ShadowRoot.referenceTarget`. Please also mention that *fire an event* gains a *relatedTarget* parameter, that the legacy target override flag became a *legacyTargetOverride* `EventTarget` parameter (so HTML now passes the `Document` itself), and that *clone a node* copies the reference target. Linking WICG/webcomponents#1086 and #1098 would also help.\n\n</details>\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
